# KServe Controller Reconcile Lag

This monitor detects controller reconcile lag above **{{threshold}} seconds** for [{{labels.service_name}}](/#/components/{{componentUrnForUrl}}).

Compare the metric and threshold in this monitor's chart at the time of the alert.

Triage:

1. Inspect the controller for errors or throttling:
   `kubectl logs -n <kserve-namespace> deploy/kserve-controller-manager -c manager --tail=100`.
2. Check the controller pod for CPU/memory pressure:
   `kubectl top pod -n <kserve-namespace> -l control-plane=kserve-controller-manager`.
3. Inspect the KServe workqueues in Prometheus, selecting `suse_ai_product="kserve"`
   and the affected `service_namespace` and `service_name`. Group by `name`:
   `workqueue_depth` shows waiting work and
   `workqueue_longest_running_processor_seconds` shows the longest active item.
   `workqueue_unfinished_work_seconds` sums time across all active items and can
   exceed the alert threshold even when no individual item is stuck.
4. Confirm the InferenceServices it reconciles are healthy (stuck resources drive requeues):
   `kubectl get isvc -A`.
5. Restart the controller if it is wedged:
   `kubectl rollout restart deploy/kserve-controller-manager -n <kserve-namespace>`.
